WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.776
A text-to-image model

00:00:01.588 --> 00:00:02.578
trained for under

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.687
55 dollars

00:00:04.206 --> 00:00:05.550
A new arXiv

00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:06.894
paper Asuka-FM

00:00:07.001 --> 00:00:09.559
trains a 206-million-parameter

00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:10.774
diffusion transformer

00:00:10.586 --> 00:00:11.776
from scratch on

00:00:11.588 --> 00:00:12.826
a single RTX

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:13.498
4090

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.169
Training took about

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.728
160 hours at 512

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.235
pixels

00:00:18.306 --> 00:00:19.580
for under fifty-five

00:00:19.391 --> 00:00:20.110
dollars

00:00:20.249 --> 00:00:21.180
The author calls

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:22.159
it a micro-budget

00:00:21.971 --> 00:00:23.421
baseline for foundation

00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:23.857
models

00:00:23.929 --> 00:00:24.836
with the best

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.791
DPG score for

00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:26.475
its compute

00:00:27.014 --> 00:00:29.325
It reaches 0.609

00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:30.480
on GenEval and

00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:32.639
78.51 on DPG

00:00:32.816 --> 00:00:34.065
by tackling attention

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:34.561
costs

00:00:34.632 --> 00:00:36.176
compilation graph breaks

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.238
and the autoencoder

00:00:37.049 --> 00:00:38.440
bottleneck on consumer

00:00:38.252 --> 00:00:38.971
hardware

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:40.524
Full story on

00:00:40.335 --> 00:00:41.231
the dashboard
